WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.340
A CUDA kernel is a function that GPU threads execute.

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:07.820
In this file, global marks hello as a kernel.

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.980
The thread writes forty-two point zero at output index zero.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:18.460
On the CPU, main reserves space in GPU memory for one float.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:23.510
The first one requests one block. The second one requests one thread in that block.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.150
The argument output gives the kernel the address of the float.

00:00:29.170 --> 00:00:35.100
A streaming multiprocessor, or S M, executes instructions for the GPU thread.

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:39.185
The kernel stores forty-two point zero in GPU memory.

00:00:39.405 --> 00:00:43.505
The CPU copies the value back, and main prints it in the console.

00:00:45.525 --> 00:00:49.380
Change the value in the assignment, then compile and run again.

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.470
The launch still asks for one block and one thread.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:55.120
Which value will main print this time?
